  "text": "M184 139 137 102 178 109 204 86 213 116 247 102 222 146 188 148Z\n\nTake part in a game or activity; with an instrument, make music.\n\nThe part at the end of a leg that supports standing and walking.\n\nPip has delivered Grandma’s copy. Hear Mara’s reply at the dock.\n\nLoop has shown your ending. You can replay it whenever you like.\n\nGrandma opens The Torn Wing. There is another story to discover.\n\nPip places his chosen memory in the flower he grew with Grandma.\n\nThe original manuscript and the ending chosen for Sol to share.\n\nThe seed is travelling in the seed boat. Pip waits on the bank.\n\nMove Pip with the arrow keys or WASD. Talk to Mara at the dock.\n\nThese are your thoughts. You can change them whenever you like.\n\nGrandma has Mara’s page—and understands why she couldn’t visit.\n\nThe parts of a plant that grow into the soil and take in water.\n\nMara opens The Torn Wing for the people gathered in the garden.\n\nAn experience involving exploration, challenges or discoveries.\n\n· Your place is saved. Read the whole passage at your own pace.\n\nM257 167 233 86m44 78-23-83m-12 28 20-5m-14 24 20-5m-13 24 20-5\n\nGrandma has finished The Empty Bench. She is ready to share it.\n\nTaking part in an activity, or making music with an instrument.\n\nMoved something closer by holding it and drawing it toward you.\n\nOn one occasion; for once means on this occasion, unlike usual.\n\nMara takes tape from her dock office. Bring it back to the boy.\n\nA male person already mentioned, or something belonging to him.\n\nWalk with Rina to Sol’s workshop. She carries one loaf for him.\n\nM0 0v-62M0-12q-24-3-28-21 28 0 28 21M0-22q22-4 27-23-26 2-27 23\n\nMara’s page is called The Torn Wing. Pip is carrying her copy.\n\nAn animal with feathers and wings; here it is made from paper.",
